; DOMAIN: mathematics/number-theory/automorphic-forms [CLOSED, derived 2026-08-01]; Claim: Automorphic forms are functions on reductive groups invariant under discrete subgroups, generalizing modular forms. Key concepts include: GL(2) modular forms as holomorphic functions on upper half-plane satisfying f(gamma*z) = (cz+d)^k f(z); Maass forms as eigenfunctions of the Laplacian; automorphic representations as adelic generalizations; the Langlands program connecting automorphic representations of GL(n) to Galois representations; Eisenstein series; Hecke operators and Hecke eigenvalues; the Selberg trace formula relating spectral data to geometric data; and the adelic perspective where automorphic forms live on G(A_Q)/G(Q) with central character. Bridges to class_field_theory (Artin reciprocity as GL(1) case), zeta_function (automorphic L-functions), analytic_number_theory (prime distribution), and representation_theory.;; Modular form: holomorphic function on upper half-plane satisfying weight-k transformation under SL(2,Z)
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Function $f) (--> Holomorphic $f) (--> UpperHalfPlane $H) (--> Domain $f $H) (--> Weight $k) (--> ForAll $gamma (In $gamma (SL2Z)) (Equals (Apply $f (MobiusAction $gamma $z)) (Multiply (Power (czPlusD $gamma) $k) (Apply $f $z)))))) (--> ModularForm $f $k)) (stv 1.0 0.9)
;; Maass form: eigenfunction of Laplacian on upper half-plane invariant under discrete subgroup
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Function $f) (--> Eigenfunction $f (Laplacian $H)) (--> UpperHalfPlane $H) (--> Domain $f $H) (--> InvariantUnder $f (DiscreteSubgroup $Gamma)))) (--> MaassForm $f $Gamma)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Eisenstein series: sum over cosets of modular group, convergent for weight-k holomorphic forms
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Series $E) (--> SumOver $E (Cosets $Gamma $SL2Z)) (--> Convergent $E) (--> ModularForm $E $k))) (--> EisensteinSeries $E $k)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Hecke operator: acts on space of modular forms, self-adjoint wrt Petersson inner product, eigenvalues encode arithmetic data
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Operator $T_n) (--> ActsOn $T_n (SpaceOf $f (ModularForm $f $k))) (--> SelfAdjoint $T_n (PeterssonInnerProduct)) (--> Eigenvalue $lambda (Apply $T_n $f)))) (--> HeckeOperator $T_n $lambda)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Adelic automorphic form: function on G(A_Q) right-invariant under G(Q), K-finite, Z-finite, moderate growth
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Function $phi) (--> ReductiveGroup $G) (--> AdeleRing $A_Q) (--> Domain $phi $G) (--> RightInvariant $phi (G $Q)) (--> KFinite $phi) (--> ZFinite $phi) (--> ModerateGrowth $phi))) (--> AdelicAutomorphicForm $phi $G)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Langlands correspondence: bijection between automorphic representations of GL(n) and irreducible Galois representations
(|- ((==> (&& (--> AutomorphicRepresentation $pi (GLn $n)) (--> GaloisRepresentation $rho) (--> Bijection $pi $rho))) (--> LanglandsCorrespondence $pi $rho)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Selberg trace formula: relates spectral data (eigenvalues of Laplacian) to geometric data (conjugacy classes)
(|- ((==> (&& (--> DiscreteSubgroup $Gamma) (--> SumOver $S (SpectralData $Gamma)) (--> SumOver $G (GeometricData $Gamma)) (--> Equals $S $G))) (--> SelbergTraceFormula $Gamma)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
